# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in from PostHog > Project settings >
# Project API key. See src/analytics.ts and docs/privacy-policy.md.
VITE_POSTHOG_PROJECT_API_KEY=

# Leave unset (or "development") for every local/test build. Set to
# "production" only in the .env used for the one build that actually gets
# zipped and uploaded to the Chrome Web Store — `vite build` alone can't tell
# that build apart from a developer's own unpacked test build, so this is the
# explicit switch that keeps dev noise out of real usage data in PostHog.
VITE_ANALYTICS_ENV=development
